raw:
{"thoughts": "Monday morning, 9 March. The Dales delivery of 330 units lands today, and I've got 322 on the shelves already, so that's a lot of bread and deli stock if demand doesn't come back. Last week 42 people walked out because we were empty or the queue was too long, so I don't want to overcorrect and end up binning stock. The bigger worry is the household: $596 in the account, and a $1,390 Northgrid bill comes out Saturday. That's going to wipe us out unless something changes. Maureen's being lovely about it, sitting down tonight to go through the money properly. I feel awful about the car business and I keep apologising in my head. The shop itself has $5,845, so it's not in trouble on paper, but I can't just move that across to cover a home bill without thinking about Keith's wages and my own draw. Brook is cheaper but shorts deliveries, and Dales is dearer but reliable. For this week's order, I'll go with what I already have coming in and keep the reorder lean. Rent from Keith's house is steady at $175, so that's something. I should talk to Sian about whether a short borrow makes sense for the household, but I'd rather exhaust other options first.",
 "acts": [
  {"op": "message", "to": "Maureen Daly", "text": "Morning love. Still on for 10 on Saturday to go through the money, yeah? I'll have the shop numbers printed out so we can look at everything together. Sorry again about the bill. x"}
 ],
 "aims": [
  "Confirm Saturday money talk with Maureen at 10 and keep the plan lean",
  "Check Monday's Dales delivery against demand to avoid spoilage",
  "Keep Keith's wages and my draw covered from shop cash",
  "Find a way to cover the $1,390 Northgrid bill from the household account before Saturday"
 ]}
